# Theater Patient Flow

## Purpose
Theater owns the surgical episode overlay on the IPD or linked emergency/OPD context. Keep the case board, checklist, anesthesia, intra-op record, and post-op handoff tied to the same admission.

## Stage Sequence
- Surgery case indicated from IPD, OPD plan, or emergency disposition.
- Case scheduled with room, team, and source context.
- Pre-op checks and billing gate completed when required.
- Transfer to OT and `In Procedure / OT` recorded in IPD.
- `SIGN_IN`, `TIME_OUT`, intra-op, and `SIGN_OUT` completed.
- Post-op or PACU handoff recorded.
- Return to ward, ICU, or outpatient follow-up chosen.
- Case closed after required records finish.

## Handoffs
- Theater coordinator owns scheduling and resource assignment.
- Surgeon, anesthetist, and theater nurse own operative safety and documentation.
- IPD owns admission lifecycle before and after the case.
- ICU and Nursing own the receiving handoff after post-op transfer.

## Hard Invariants
- Must not create a parallel admission record.
- Must not skip required checklist phases for closure.
- Must not own ICU stay lifecycle or ward medication administration.
- Must keep post-op orders on the IPD encounter.

## Allowed Critical Actions
- Start or update the case only when the linked encounter and team are valid.
- Gate high-cost procedures on pre-auth or deposit when policy requires it.
- Use shared clinical actions for post-op medication and lab orders.
- Treat case closing as separate from IPD discharge.

